Ladybird allows mlock() and munlock() to the processes that load a GPU
driver, and refuses mlockall() and mlock2(). Chromium allows mlock and
munlock to every process, and puts mlockall and munlockall in its
restricted set: SyscallSets::IsAllowedAddressSpaceAccess() lists them
that way. Firefox’s SandboxFilter.cpp allows mlock and munlock too, and
neither engine allows mlock2. From reading the sources.
